@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Catalog
+
+For whoever changes pantry searches or enables their cache. Catalog searches return matching items in name order,
+with a disposable cache added after the item page was reported slow on Saturday mornings.
+
+## Search
+
+[`items`](../../larder/catalog.py) uses the existing Postgres full-text query and returns item ids, names and stock.
+Each exact search string has its own cache key; empty results are cached too. Database errors propagate to the caller
+and are never cached. Cache read, decoding, setup and write failures log a warning and leave the database path available.
+
+## Configuration
+
+Install [`requirements.txt`](../../requirements.txt) with `python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt`. Set
+`REDIS_URL` in each web process, for example `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0` when Tom runs Redis locally. Restart the web
+processes after changing configuration. An absent or empty URL disables caching, including the Redis client import.
+Use a Redis database dedicated to this installation so deployments with different Postgres databases do not share results.
+The repository contains no server deployment configuration; the environment must be set by the operator.
+
+The client is reused within each process. Connect and socket timeouts are 100 ms, with client retries disabled,
+following the [redis-py connection and retry interface](https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/clients/redis-py/connect/).
+URL query parameters can override the client's connection defaults; omit such overrides to retain those limits.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Search results, including stock, expire after 15 seconds from cache insertion. There is no write invalidation;
+  disable the cache when searches require fresh stock on every request. Cached stock must not authorize an order.
+- A cache miss still executes the original query, and simultaneous misses can repeat it. Measure Saturday query
+  plans and cache hit rates before attributing the slowdown to a particular database operation.
+- Redis outages return traffic to Postgres. Clear `REDIS_URL` and restart the web processes to bypass Redis entirely.
+
+## Shaped by
+
+- [Use a disposable catalog cache](../adr/0003-use-a-disposable-catalog-cache.md)
